hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"91","It is narrated from Sabrah Juhani (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade (temporary) marriage (mut‘ah) and said: ""Beware! This (mut‘ah) is forbidden for you from this day of yours until the Day of Resurrection. And whoever has given anything should not take it back."
"92","Hazrat Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every religion has a distinguishing characteristic, and the distinguishing characteristic of Islam is modesty."
"93","Rabee’ bin Sabrah Al-Juhani narrated, his father said, I contracted Mut’ah marriage with a woman from Banu ‘Amir in exchange for two red garments during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade us from Mut’ah marriage. Muhammad bin Muslim said, I heard Rabee’ bin Sabrah narrate this to Umar bin Abdul Aziz (may Allah have mercy on him) while I was sitting with them."
